3. Natural Earth
----------------

The coastlines on the Earth models (Earth's layers, seasons) come from
Natural Earth (https://www.naturalearthdata.com), which is in the public domain.


4. Other people's models and pictures
-------------------------------------

- Coronavirus (assets/viewer3d/models/virus.*): "SARS-CoV-2 Virion (PathogenAR
  Version)", NIAID, NIH 3D entry 3DPX-014820 (https://3d.nih.gov/entries/3DPX-014820),
  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International. KINETIX split it by colour into
  the envelope and the two forms of the spike protein and simplified it.
- Globe (globe.*): NASA Earth Observatory, Blue Marble: Next Generation
  (Reto Stöckli), public domain.
- Landforms (landforms.*): heights from Terrain Tiles on AWS
  (https://registry.opendata.aws/terrain-tiles/), containing SRTM and GMTED2010
  data courtesy of the U.S. Geological Survey and NASA, and ETOPO1 (NOAA), public
  domain; the delta picture is from NASA Worldview/GIBS (MODIS Aqua), public domain.
- Compound microscope (microscope.*): "Omax compound microscope" by 3Donimus,
  from Poly Pizza (https://poly.pizza/m/dcuaH6bEkwn), Creative Commons
  Attribution 3.0. KINETIX removed the display stand and cord and grouped the
  pieces into named parts.
- Inner ear (ear.*: cochlea, vestibule, semicircular canals): micro-CT surface of
  specimen F07, "Human Bony Labyrinth: Co-Registered CT and micro-CT Images, Surface
  Models and Anatomical Landmarks", W. Wimmer, L. Anschuetz, S. Weder, F. Wagner,
  H. Delingette, M. Caversaccio (2019), https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.3355272,
  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International. KINETIX simplified it, split it into
  three parts and placed it in the ear with the BodyParts3D pinna.
- DNA atoms (dna.*, "every atom"): PDB entry 1BNA (Drew, Wing, Takano, Broka, Tanaka,
  Itakura, Dickerson, 1981), RCSB Protein Data Bank (https://www.rcsb.org), CC0.
- Downloaded on first use (remote_models/, not in the app): woolly mammoth,
  Cosmic Buddha and Apollo 11 command module from Smithsonian Open Access
  (https://3d.si.edu), CC0; Saturn V, Apollo Lunar Module and Hubble from NASA 3D
  Resources (https://github.com/nasa/NASA-3D-Resources), public domain, split into
  named parts with their own pictures; liver and stomach from BodyParts3D (CC BY 4.0).

The full list with links is in docs/licensing/3D_MODELS.md.


5. Built by KINETIX
-------------------

All other models (cells, neuron, flower, DNA, electric motor, prism, bar
magnet, atoms, molecules, solids and nets, Earth's layers, volcano, solar
system, seasons, atomic orbitals, hybridisation, crystal lattices, electric
circuit, AC generator, transformer, simple machines, nephron, engine,
gears, lens bench, laboratory apparatus, the middle ear, the inside of the
kidney, the downloadable tooth, skin, bacterium and mitochondrion, and the
simplified Taj Mahal, Qutub Minar, India Gate and Konark Sun Temple) are built
in code by KINETIX (tool/models/recipes) and use no downloaded assets.

The build tools (tool/models) use three.js, esbuild, glTF-Transform,
meshoptimizer, draco3dgltf and sharp as development dependencies only (see
tool/models/package.json).
